{
  "_readme": "Two-layer token architecture. Layer 1 (primitive) is raw values. Layer 2 (semantic) maps roles onto primitives. CSS: --nil-primitive-* raw, --nil-* consumer. Components only reference --nil-*. Canvas, accent and the rest are defined in primitive.color below; do not restate values in prose, they go stale. Brutalist: 4px default radius (soft brutalist), 2px borders. Generated CSS: npm run tokens:build Chart colours (color-chart-*): four categorical colours (blue, pale blue, orange, pale orange) and a five-step ramp. Every chart mark takes a --nil-color-border outline at --nil-border-width. The OUTLINE clears 3:1 against the page, not the fill, so the pale fills are below 3:1 on purpose. Text on a filled swatch uses the matching *-text token (4.5:1, checked by tokens:validate). More than four categories: group the rest into Other or label them. Do not add colours. Success green stays for wins.",
